# The F/P's first job node, and the branch's payoff for a book that has spent
# every advancement laying poison. Fifteen orbs from another dimension, one
# more for every burn stack already standing on the group, up to twenty-five.
#
# Scatter is the shape -- the same one Megiddo Flame uses. Each orb hunts its
# own enemy and the ones that double up keep 55% of their final damage, so a
# crowd takes an orb apiece and a lone boss takes the lot. GMS sends them at
# the boss with the highest HP first, which is what the spare strikes going to
# the healthiest already is.
#
# The count is what makes this the F/P's own skill rather than another nuke.
# Opened on a fresh fight it throws fifteen; thrown after Poison Mist, Ifrit,
# Inferno Aura and whatever the rotation is swinging, it throws twenty or more,
# and on a map where every mob is burning it sits at the cap. Read live off the
# group each time, so the chooser learns the wait is worth more once the
# poisons are down.
#
# GMS's `time 20` is how long an orb hunts before it expires, not a beat to
# land them on: the client publishes no interval, so all of them land together.
name: "DoT Punisher"
description:
  "Summons flame orbs from another dimension to pursue enemies. The flame "
  "orbs target the boss with the highest HP first. The number of orbs you "
  "summon depends on how many damage-over-time stacks you have on enemies."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ATTACK
tags: SKILL_TAG_FIRE
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_FIRE_POISON_ARCH_MAGE_V skill_order: 1 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_JOB
max_level: 30
required_equip_type: EQUIP_TYPE_STAFF
base_delay_ms: 510
cooldown_seconds: 25.0
max_enemies: 25
lines: 5
base { skill_pct: 4.15 }
per_level { skill_pct: 0.15 }
scatter {
  hits: 15
  repeat_final_dmg_pct: -0.45
  hits_per_dot: 1.0
  max_hits: 25
}
dot {
  interval_seconds: 1.0
  duration_seconds: 8.0
  lines: 1
  base { skill_pct: 2.03 }
  per_level { skill_pct: 0.03 }
}
